# clock Changelog

## 1.2.0

- Fix the entry point (`libs` -> `lib`); the app now starts again
- Read the clock once per run, so output can no longer mix two ticks
- Zero-padded output (`09:05:03` instead of `9:5:3`)
- Add `--format/-f` (any `strftime` pattern) and `--utc/-u`
- `_clock` helpers accept an optional moment; `mint()` kept as a deprecated alias
- Drop the bogus `datetime` dependency (it ships with Python)
- Add unit tests, `.gitignore` and a proper README
- Remove the duplicate `Readme` file (same content as `README.md`)

## 1.0.0  2026-05-26

- Initial release
